Consider the memoized 0/1 knapsack below. First compute the optimal value for capacity 5, then count how many distinct (i, c) states the cache actually misses on (each miss is one state evaluation).

```python
w = [2, 3, 4]
v = [3, 4, 5]
C = 5
from functools import lru_cache
@lru_cache(maxsize=None)
def dp(i, c):
    if i == len(w) or c == 0:
        return 0
    if w[i] > c:
        return dp(i + 1, c)
    return max(dp(i + 1, c), v[i] + dp(i + 1, c - w[i]))
print(dp(0, 5))
print(dp.cache_info().misses)
```

Output only the two numbers, one per line.
